# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as LF on every
# platform. Two things depend on that rather than merely preferring it.
#
# The examples and the generated library are embedded in the assembly, and a server
# compares what it would write against what is already on disk — outright for an
# example, by the build marker in the header for the library. A checkout carrying
# CRLF would embed CRLF, so the same commit built on Windows and on Linux would
# produce different resources and write Windows line endings into a Linux server's
# folder.
#
# The scripts in scripts/ are run by /bin/sh, which does not accept a CR at the end
# of a line.
*               text=auto eol=lf

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.lua           text eol=lf
